# ============================================================================
# campaign-site  ·  teams.doviloop.dev
#
# Copy to .env.local for local work, and paste the same five into the Vercel
# project under Settings > Environment Variables (Production and Preview).
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in .env. .env and .env.local are gitignored.
# Every one of these is safe to be public: they are all client-side VITE_
# values, baked into the bundle at build time and visible in the browser.
# Nothing here is a secret, and no secret should ever be added to this file.
#
# The page works with all five empty. Each one degrades to something sensible,
# so a missing value never produces a broken page or a lost lead.
# ============================================================================


# 1. Where the qualifier POSTs the lead.
#    WHERE IT COMES FROM: Batch F, repo campaign-n8n. Import the workflow into
#    n8n, open the Webhook node, copy its Production URL.
#    Shape of the body is fixed in campaign-specs/00-START-HERE.md and is
#    implemented in src/lib/contract.ts. Do not change one without the other.
#    IF EMPTY: the form POSTs to same-origin /api/lead, which `npm run mock`
#    answers locally. In production an empty value means every lead lands in
#    the localStorage recovery queue instead of n8n, so set this before launch.
VITE_LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL=

# 2. The booking page a qualified lead is sent to.
#    WHERE IT COMES FROM: Google Calendar appointment schedule. Calendar >
#    Create > Appointment schedule, 09:00 to 17:00 CET plus the US evening
#    block, then Share > copy the booking page link.
#    IF EMPTY: the confirmation screen falls back to a mailto so a qualified
#    lead still has a way to reach you.
VITE_BOOKING_URL=

# 3. PostHog project API key.
#    WHERE IT COMES FROM: posthog.com, EU cloud, Project settings > Project API
#    key. It starts with phc_. This is a write-only ingest key and is meant to
#    be public. Do NOT put a personal API key here.
#    IF EMPTY: analytics is not initialised at all. No script is loaded and no
#    request is made. In dev the events print to the console instead.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=

# 4. PostHog ingestion host.
#    WHERE IT COMES FROM: fixed by which PostHog cloud the project lives in.
#    The campaign runs on EU cloud, so this should stay as the EU host below.
#    Only change it if the project is moved.
#    IF EMPTY: defaults to https://eu.i.posthog.com in src/lib/env.ts.
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com

# 5. Meta pixel ID.
#    WHERE IT COMES FROM: Meta Business Manager > Events Manager > Data
#    sources > your pixel. It is a 15 or 16 digit number.
#    The same ID goes on doviloop.dev as well, otherwise the retargeting
#    audience only ever sees people who landed on this campaign page.
#    IF EMPTY: the pixel is completely inert. Nothing is injected, no request
#    is made, no cookie is written. That is deliberate for EU consent reasons.
VITE_META_PIXEL_ID=
